{%- comment -%}
  Cart progress toward free shipping and up to three discount tiers.

  Everything here is computed from the real cart total against thresholds the
  merchant sets. The discount codes named must actually exist in Shopify —
  Liquid cannot verify that, so the setting says so plainly. A bar that
  promises a code checkout rejects is worse than no bar at all.

  Free shipping and the tiers are one sorted list, not two — a merchant can put
  free shipping above or below a tier and the bar still reads left to right.

  The milestones are spaced evenly along the track rather than by their money
  value. Scaled to the largest goal, ₹500 against a ₹9,999 top tier sat at 5%
  and the first reward looked unreachable; even segments make early progress
  feel like progress, which is the whole point of the bar. Each milestone sits
  at the centre of its own segment, which is also the centre of its label
  column below — so a node and its caption line up by construction rather than
  by two sets of numbers that have to be kept in step.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ship_threshold = settings.free_shipping_threshold | default: 0 | times: 100

  comment
    One record per milestone: a zero-padded amount to sort on, then the real
    amount in paise, the kind, the reward label and the discount code. Padded
    because Liquid sorts lexicographically, so 900 would otherwise sort above
    1000. Records are separated by a double semicolon and fields by a pipe, and
    both are stripped out of merchant copy before it goes in.

    Quote characters are kept out of every comment inside a liquid tag on
    purpose: the tag is tokenised line by line, and a stray quote in prose ends
    up opening a string that never closes.
  endcomment
  assign rows = ''

  if ship_threshold > 0
    assign lbl = settings.free_shipping_short | default: 'Free shipping' | replace: '|', ' ' | replace: ';;', ' '
    assign pad = ship_threshold | prepend: '000000000000' | slice: -12, 12
    assign rows = rows | append: pad | append: '|' | append: ship_threshold | append: '|ship|' | append: lbl | append: '|'
  endif

  for i in (1..3)
    case i
      when 1
        assign amt = settings.tier_1_amount
        assign lbl = settings.tier_1_label
        assign cde = settings.tier_1_code
      when 2
        assign amt = settings.tier_2_amount
        assign lbl = settings.tier_2_label
        assign cde = settings.tier_2_code
      when 3
        assign amt = settings.tier_3_amount
        assign lbl = settings.tier_3_label
        assign cde = settings.tier_3_code
    endcase
    if amt != blank and amt > 0
      assign cents = amt | times: 100
      assign pad = cents | prepend: '000000000000' | slice: -12, 12
      assign lbl = lbl | default: '' | replace: '|', ' ' | replace: ';;', ' '
      assign cde = cde | default: '' | strip | replace: '|', '' | replace: ';;', ''
      comment
        The separator goes between records, never after the last one. A
        trailing one leaves an empty record whose survival depends on how the
        engine treats trailing blanks in split, and an empty record renders as
        a phantom milestone at zero.
      endcomment
      if rows != blank
        assign rows = rows | append: ';;'
      endif
      assign rows = rows | append: pad | append: '|' | append: cents | append: '|tier|' | append: lbl | append: '|' | append: cde
    endif
  endfor

  assign milestones = rows | split: ';;' | sort
  assign count = milestones.size
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The merchant's copy, with the theme's wording as the fallback. Resolved once,
  up here, rather than at each of the half-dozen places it is used: the status
  line below and the data attributes the script re-renders it from have to say
  the same thing, and a default repeated six times is a default that drifts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ship_prefix = settings.free_shipping_away_text | default: "You're" -%}
{%- assign ship_suffix = settings.free_shipping_away_suffix | default: 'away from free shipping' -%}
{%- assign ship_won = settings.free_shipping_reached_text | default: 'Free shipping unlocked' -%}
{%- assign tier_prefix = settings.tier_away_text | default: 'Add' -%}
{%- assign tier_suffix = settings.tier_away_suffix | default: 'more to unlock' -%}

{%- if settings.cart_promo_text != blank -%}
  <p class="cart-promo body-upper">{{ settings.cart_promo_text }}</p>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if count > 0 -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      Fill is piecewise across the segments: within a segment it interpolates on
      the money still owed, so the bar creeps forward with every item rather
      than jumping a whole segment at a time. Past the last milestone it runs to
      the end of the track — a bar stopped short of full when everything is
      unlocked reads as unfinished.
    endcomment
    assign total = cart.total_price
    assign fill = 0
    assign prev_amt = 0
    assign prev_pos = 0
    assign resolved = false
    assign next_amt = 0
    assign next_kind = ''
    assign next_label = ''
    assign next_code = ''

    for row in milestones
      assign parts = row | split: '|'
      assign at = parts[1] | plus: 0
      assign pos = forloop.index0 | times: 2 | plus: 1 | times: 5000 | divided_by: count | divided_by: 100.0
      unless resolved
        if total < at
          assign span = at | minus: prev_amt
          assign gap = pos | minus: prev_pos
          if span > 0
            assign into = total | minus: prev_amt | times: 1.0
            assign fill = into | divided_by: span | times: gap | plus: prev_pos
          else
            assign fill = prev_pos
          endif
          assign resolved = true
          assign next_amt = at
          assign next_kind = parts[2]
          assign next_label = parts[3]
          assign next_code = parts[4] | default: ''
        endif
      endunless
      assign prev_amt = at
      assign prev_pos = pos
    endfor
    unless resolved
      assign fill = 100
    endunless
    comment
      Two decimals is plenty for a width, and keeps the inline style readable.
    endcomment
    assign fill = fill | times: 100 | round | divided_by: 100.0

    comment
      The status line is rendered here as well as recomputed in JS. Left to the
      script alone the drawer opened with an empty line that filled in a beat
      later, which both flashes and shifts everything under it.
    endcomment
    if resolved
      assign away = next_amt | minus: total | money
      if next_kind == 'ship'
        capture status
          echo ship_prefix
          echo ' '
          echo away
          echo ' '
          echo ship_suffix
        endcapture
      else
        capture status
          echo tier_prefix
          echo ' '
          echo away
          echo ' '
          echo tier_suffix
          echo ' '
          echo next_label
          if next_code != blank
            echo ' with code '
            echo next_code
          endif
        endcapture
      endif
    else
      comment
        Nothing left ahead: name everything unlocked rather than going blank.
      endcomment
      assign won = ''
      for row in milestones
        assign parts = row | split: '|'
        if parts[2] == 'ship'
          assign won_part = ship_won
        else
          assign won_part = parts[3]
        endif
        if won != blank
          assign won = won | append: ' · '
        endif
        assign won = won | append: won_part
      endfor
      assign status = won
    endif
  -%}

  <div class="cart-progress{% if resolved == false %} is-complete{% endif %}" data-cart-progress
       data-prefix="{{ ship_prefix | escape }}"
       data-suffix="{{ ship_suffix | escape }}"
       data-reached="{{ ship_won | escape }}"
       data-tier-prefix="{{ tier_prefix | escape }}"
       data-tier-suffix="{{ tier_suffix | escape }}"
       style="--cart-progress-cols: {{ count }}">

    <p class="cart-progress_text body-upper" data-cart-progress-text>{{ status }}</p>

    <div class="cart-progress_track" role="progressbar" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100"
         aria-valuenow="{{ fill | round }}" aria-label="{{ status | strip | escape }}">
      <span class="cart-progress_fill" data-cart-progress-fill style="width: {{ fill }}%"></span>
      {%- for row in milestones -%}
        {%- assign parts = row | split: '|' -%}
        {%- assign at = parts[1] | plus: 0 -%}
        {%- assign pos = forloop.index0 | times: 2 | plus: 1 | times: 5000 | divided_by: count | divided_by: 100.0 -%}
        <span class="cart-progress_node{% if cart.total_price >= at %} is-reached{% endif %}"
              style="left: {{ pos }}%" data-node="{{ at }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      One legend column per milestone, so every caption sits directly under its
      own node however many milestones the merchant has switched on.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="cart-progress_legend">
      {%- for row in milestones -%}
        {%- assign parts = row | split: '|' -%}
        {%- assign at = parts[1] | plus: 0 -%}
        {%- assign pos = forloop.index0 | times: 2 | plus: 1 | times: 5000 | divided_by: count | divided_by: 100.0 -%}
        <span class="cart-milestone{% if cart.total_price >= at %} is-reached{% endif %}"
              data-tier="{{ at }}" data-pos="{{ pos }}" data-kind="{{ parts[2] }}"
              data-label="{{ parts[3] | escape }}" data-code="{{ parts[4] | default: '' | escape }}">
          <span class="cart-milestone_amount body-upper">{{ at | money }}</span>
          <span class="cart-milestone_label body-upper">{{ parts[3] }}</span>
        </span>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
